Z||000006||qwikgta||08-28-2001||10:20 PM||||I have thought about this too.  Start with a 3-6 inch rear frame extention kit like some of the lambo/ferrari kits use.  Start to modify the body panels, wide in the back and cut the front short, again like the lambo kit does.  Glass a spoiler into the rear and some ground effects/side scoops.  Then just glass it all up, n' paint it and create your own look.  You will need to lower it, add 17-18" rims and redo the brakes.  As for engines, do the baby N* to be diff.   Now if I just had the $$$$$$ and the time.  :-)<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
