Z||000009||DreXteR||08-29-2001||08:40 PM||||RedOktober - Where you find that?? I like it, need more info about it. As far I can see is no specific kit. It has a super front suspesion, no interiors or engine. Basically its for a mid engine. Also has a very nice hole in the front for cooling and can be used to increase the downfroce. Huge rear air intakes and possible a good air flow path to out side. Its just perfect!<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000010||RedOktober||08-31-2001||01:15 AM||||I think someone already posted the address. But this is just an example of what could be done.<P>What I would like to see the next Fiero to be is a cross between what the new MR2 is and the fun to drive of our cars now along with refinement in technologies that have occured in the last 13+years since our cars were produced. <BR>Imagine a car that you would build from a beat up donor. Just drop the rear cradle, gas tank, seats, and bolt in all the misc. parts from our cars into it. <P>To give you a break down:<BR>front suspension : Tubular using f body spindles, allows the use of bigger brakes and other mods.<BR>Rear suspension: control arms tubular, with GM style struts or similar to the tubular setup used in the Diablo Kits.They work great!<BR>Engine: What u want???<BR>Trans: 5 spd, auto?? Sequential shift???We can make custom transmissions for cheap, especially if it was a Manual.<BR>Body: Injection molded Plastic, From recycled drink bottles. Like the Pronto Prototype. (Negotiations with molding companies already in place) <BR>Chassis: Combination tube frame and stamped aluminum. I've found a few companies that are willing to do custom dies and stamps and limited production runs.<BR>Glass: If I can get custom made glass for a Diablo Kit, I can get the same guys to do the wind screen and side windows.<BR>Lights: I have found 5 companies that wil make the new style lights that are so popular on todays cars.<BR>Safety: Personally i do not like the concept of AirBags, but there are enough manufactures that are willing to sell em. ABS Brakes??? can be pulled off any modern GM and retrofitted to work.<BR>Volume: If lotus, Lamborghini, Ferarri, and even our Home grown Steve Millen can build a super car and make a profit, then a good break even point would be about 250-500 cars a year.<BR>Price: Under 10,000 for a complete CRATED Shell.(U build it with a $1000 donor and a few beer buddies) About 18,000-22,000 for a complete Turkey.(Customer options can cause price to vary). <BR>Assembly: Probably in South east Asia. Only way to keep costs down, unless you can find Noth American workers to work for $750/Mo.<BR>Leagality: No matter what the car is called or how the buyer wishes to have it delivered, they would still ave to come to the assemby plant to assist in the construction(What better way to spend 2 weeks holidays).<BR>Racing: A Fiero racing series can be established as a SPEC series. All cars equal its up to the drivers and their teams to tune it for more speed.<BR>Whats Next: negotiatins with the Transmission builders(ongoing), Venture Capitalists and Money Men (Jan 5, 2002), and to establish a smal team of Skunk Works that are commited to building something fabulous(needed NOW). Designers, Machinists( to train the workers),someone who is willing to relocate for a few years, Managers, Marketers, Etc. I'm sure You could fit in somewhere.<P>If you have read this far... Thank you.<BR>If you are interested.... the line form over to the right, no pushing please.<BR>   <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/red6[1]a.jpg">  <BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"<p>[This message has been edited by RedOktober (edited 08-31-2001).]||||reg||1
